IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc5-s131-to-143.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada): PART IV, the sub-heading "Misleading Justice" (sections 131 to 143). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) or a core type. JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING otherwise.
-- Terms defined in section 118 (judicial proceeding, evidence, witness) are INPUTS typed MAYBE BOOLEAN, named `s 118 <term>: ...` (the answers of ccc5-s118-to-130-1.l4).

§ `Part IV -- Misleading Justice (ss 131-143)`

§§ `s 131 Perjury`

-- src:2861 | (3) Subsections (1) and (1.1) do not apply to a statement referred to in either of those subsections that is made by a person who is not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make that statement.
@ref s 131(3) (src:2861)
GIVEN `the statement is made by a person who is not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make that statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(3) subsections (1) and (1.1) do not apply to a statement made by a person not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the statement is made by a person who is not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make that statement` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2855 | 131 (1) Subject to subsection (3), every one commits perjury who, with intent to mislead, makes before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before him a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally, knowing that the statement is false.
-- src:2861 | (3) Subsections (1) and (1.1) do not apply to a statement referred to in either of those subsections that is made by a person who is not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make that statement.
@ref s 131(1) (src:2855-2861)
GIVEN `the person makes the statement before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 131(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1) the person commits perjury by a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 131(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply"
        IF `the person makes the statement before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before them` AND `it is a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally` AND `the person acts with intent to mislead` AND `the person knows that the statement is false` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2857 | (1.1) Subject to subsection (3), every person who gives evidence under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act, or gives evidence or a statement pursuant to an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act, commits perjury who, with intent to mislead, makes a false statement knowing that it is false, whether or not the false statement was made under oath or solemn affirmation in accordance with subsection (1), so long as the false statement was made in accordance with any formalities required by the law of the place outside Canada in which the person is virtually present or heard.
-- src:2861 | (3) Subsections (1) and (1.1) do not apply to a statement referred to in either of those subsections that is made by a person who is not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make that statement.
@ref s 131(1.1) (src:2857-2861)
GIVEN `the person gives evidence under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gives evidence or a statement pursuant to an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes a false statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the false statement was made otherwise than in accordance with the formalities required by the law of the place outside Canada in which the person is virtually present or heard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 131(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the false statement was made under oath or solemn affirmation in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1.1) the person commits perjury by a false statement given by video link or under a mutual legal assistance order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the false statement was made otherwise than in accordance with the formalities required by the law of the place outside Canada in which the person is virtually present or heard` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as the false statement was made in accordance with any formalities required by the law of the place outside Canada in which the person is virtually present or heard"
        IF (`the answer of s 131(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply"
        IF (`the person gives evidence under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act` OR `the person gives evidence or a statement pursuant to an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act`) AND `the person makes a false statement` AND `the person acts with intent to mislead` AND `the person knows that the statement is false` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2859 | (2) Subsection (1) applies, whether or not a statement referred to in that subsection is made in a judicial proceeding.
