-- src:2855 | 131 (1) Subject to subsection (3), every one commits perjury who, with intent to mislead, makes before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before him a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally, knowing that the statement is false.
-- src:2857 | (1.1) Subject to subsection (3), every person who gives evidence under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act, or gives evidence or a statement pursuant to an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act, commits perjury who, with intent to mislead, makes a false statement knowing that it is false, whether or not the false statement was made under oath or solemn affirmation in accordance with subsection (1), so long as the false statement was made in accordance with any formalities required by the law of the place outside Canada in which the person is virtually present or heard.
@ref s 131 (src:2855-2857)
GIVEN `the answer of s 131(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 131(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131 the person commits perjury` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 131(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of s 131(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section reaches only the conduct its paragraphs describe

§§ `s 132 Punishment`

-- src:2863 | 132 Every one who commits perjury is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 132 (src:2863)
GIVEN `s 131 the person commits perjury: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132 the person who commits perjury is guilty of an indictable offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 131 the person commits perjury: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2863 | 132 Every one who commits perjury is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 132 (src:2863)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 132 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:2863 | 132 Every one who commits perjury is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 132 (src:2863)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 132 the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `by indictment`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no minimum
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine

§§ `s 133 Corroboration`

-- src:2865 | 133 No person shall be convicted of an offence under section 132 on the evidence of only one witness unless the evidence of that witness is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates the accused.
@ref s 133 (src:2865)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence under section 132` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is that of only one witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence of that witness is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133 the accused is barred from being convicted of perjury on the evidence of only one witness unless it is corroborated in a material particular` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the evidence of that witness is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the evidence of that witness is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates the accused"
        IF `the accused is charged with an offence under section 132` AND `the evidence is that of only one witness` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

