-- src:2867 | 134 (1) Subject to subsection (2), every one who, not being specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make a statement under oath or solemn affirmation, makes such a statement, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before him, knowing that the statement is false, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:2869 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a statement referred to in that subsection that is made in the course of a criminal investigation.
@ref s 134(1) (src:2867-2869)
GIVEN `the person is specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make a statement under oath or solemn affirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes such a statement, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 134(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(1) the person makes a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation without being permitted, authorized or required by law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 134(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply"
        IF (NOT `the person is specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make a statement under oath or solemn affirmation`) AND `the person makes such a statement, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before them` AND `the person knows that the statement is false` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2867 | 134 (1) Subject to subsection (2), every one who, not being specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make a statement under oath or solemn affirmation, makes such a statement, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before him, knowing that the statement is false, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 134(1) (src:2867)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 134(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:2867 | 134 (1) Subject to subsection (2), every one who, not being specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make a statement under oath or solemn affirmation, makes such a statement, by affidavit, solemn declaration or deposition or orally before a person who is authorized by law to permit it to be made before him, knowing that the statement is false, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
