§§ `s 136 Witness giving contradictory evidence`

-- src:2876 | (2) Notwithstanding the definition evidence in section 118, evidence, for the purposes of this section, does not include evidence that is not material.
@ref s 136(2) (src:2876)
GIVEN `s 118 evidence or statement: it is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(2) the evidence is evidence for the purposes of section 136` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the evidence is material`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include evidence that is not material"
        IF (`s 118 evidence or statement: it is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2874 | (1.1) Evidence given under section 714.1, 714.2 or 714.3 or under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act or evidence or a statement given under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act is deemed to be evidence given by a witness in a judicial proceeding for the purposes of subsection (1).
@ref s 136(1.1) (src:2874)
GIVEN `the evidence was given under section 714.1, 714.2 or 714.3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence was given under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence or statement was given under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1.1) the evidence is deemed to be evidence given by a witness in a judicial proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the evidence was given under section 714.1, 714.2 or 714.3` OR `the evidence was given under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act` OR `the evidence or statement was given under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2872 | 136 (1) Every one who, being a witness in a judicial proceeding, gives evidence with respect to any matter of fact or knowledge and who subsequently, in a judicial proceeding, gives evidence that is contrary to his previous evidence is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years, whether or not the prior or later evidence or either is true, but no person shall be convicted under this section unless the court, judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, is satisfied beyond a reasonable doubt that the accused, in giving evidence in either of the judicial proceedings, intended to mislead.
@ref s 136(1) (src:2872)
GIVEN `s 118 judicial proceeding: the proceeding is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 118 witness: the person was one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person, being a witness in a judicial proceeding, gives evidence with respect to a matter of fact or knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person subsequently, in a judicial proceeding, gives evidence that is contrary to their previous evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 136(2) the earlier evidence is evidence for this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 136(2) the later evidence is evidence for this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied beyond a reasonable doubt that the accused, in giving evidence in either of the judicial proceedings, intended to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prior or the later evidence, or either, is true` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1) the witness is guilty of giving contradictory evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the court is satisfied beyond a reasonable doubt that the accused, in giving evidence in either of the judicial proceedings, intended to mislead`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court, judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, is satisfied beyond a reasonable doubt that the accused, in giving evidence in either of the judicial proceedings, intended to mislead"
        IF (`s 118 judicial proceeding: the proceeding is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 118 witness: the person was one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person, being a witness in a judicial proceeding, gives evidence with respect to a matter of fact or knowledge` AND `the person subsequently, in a judicial proceeding, gives evidence that is contrary to their previous evidence` AND (`s 136(2) the earlier evidence is evidence for this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 136(2) the later evidence is evidence for this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2878 | (2.1) Where a person is charged with an offence under this section, a certificate specifying with reasonable particularity the proceeding in which that person is alleged to have given the evidence in respect of which the offence is charged, is evidence that it was given in a judicial proceeding, without proof of the signature or official character of the person by whom the certificate purports to be signed if it purports to be signed by the clerk of the court or other official having the custody of the record of that proceeding or by his lawful deputy.
@ref s 136(2.1) (src:2878)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under section 136` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate specifies with reasonable particularity the proceeding in which the person is alleged to have given the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate purports to be signed by the clerk of the court or other official having the custody of the record of that proceeding, or by their lawful deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(2.1) a certificate is evidence that the evidence was given in a judicial proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is charged with an offence under section 136` AND `the certificate specifies with reasonable particularity the proceeding in which the person is alleged to have given the evidence` AND `the certificate purports to be signed by the clerk of the court or other official having the custody of the record of that proceeding, or by their lawful deputy` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

