§§ `s 138 Offences relating to affidavits`

-- src:2884 | 138 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:2885 | (a) signs a writing that purports to be an affidavit or statutory declaration and to have been sworn or declared before him when the writing was not so sworn or declared or when he knows that he has no authority to administer the oath or declaration,
@ref s 138(a) (src:2884-2885)
GIVEN `the person signs a writing that purports to be an affidavit or statutory declaration and to have been sworn or declared before them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing was not so sworn or declared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that they have no authority to administer the oath or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(a) the person signs a writing that purports to be an affidavit or statutory declaration sworn or declared before them when it was not` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person signs a writing that purports to be an affidavit or statutory declaration and to have been sworn or declared before them` AND (`the writing was not so sworn or declared` OR `the person knows that they have no authority to administer the oath or declaration`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2884 | 138 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:2886 | (b) uses or offers for use any writing purporting to be an affidavit or statutory declaration that he knows was not sworn or declared, as the case may be, by the affiant or declarant or before a person authorized in that behalf, or
@ref s 138(b) (src:2884-2886)
GIVEN `the person uses or offers for use a writing purporting to be an affidavit or statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it was not sworn or declared by the affiant or declarant or before a person authorized in that behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(b) the person uses or offers for use a writing purporting to be an affidavit or statutory declaration that they know was not sworn or declared` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person uses or offers for use a writing purporting to be an affidavit or statutory declaration` AND `the person knows that it was not sworn or declared by the affiant or declarant or before a person authorized in that behalf` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2884 | 138 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:2887 | (c) signs as affiant or declarant a writing that purports to be an affidavit or statutory declaration and to have been sworn or declared by him, as the case may be, when the writing was not so sworn or declared.
@ref s 138(c) (src:2884-2887)
GIVEN `the person signs as affiant or declarant a writing that purports to be an affidavit or statutory declaration and to have been sworn or declared by them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing was not so sworn or declared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(c) the person signs as affiant or declarant a writing purporting to have been sworn or declared by them when it was not` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person signs as affiant or declarant a writing that purports to be an affidavit or statutory declaration and to have been sworn or declared by them` AND `the writing was not so sworn or declared` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2884 | 138 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
@ref s 138 (src:2884)
GIVEN `the answer of s 138(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 138(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 138(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138 the person is guilty of an offence under section 138` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 138(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of s 138(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of s 138(c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section reaches only the conduct its paragraphs describe

-- src:2884 | 138 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
