§§ `s 140 Public mischief`

-- src:2905 | 140 (1) Every one commits public mischief who, with intent to mislead, causes a peace officer to enter on or continue an investigation by
-- src:2906 | (a) making a false statement that accuses some other person of having committed an offence;
-- src:2907 | (b) doing anything intended to cause some other person to be suspected of having committed an offence that the other person has not committed, or to divert suspicion from himself;
-- src:2908 | (c) reporting that an offence has been committed when it has not been committed; or
-- src:2909 | (d) reporting or in any other way making it known or causing it to be made known that he or some other person has died when he or that other person has not died.
@ref s 140(1) (src:2905-2909)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causes a peace officer to enter on or continue an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by making a false statement that accuses some other person of having committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by doing anything intended to cause some other person to be suspected of having committed an offence that the other person has not committed, or to divert suspicion from the person themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reporting that an offence has been committed when it has not been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reporting or in any other way making it known or causing it to be made known that the person or some other person has died when they have not died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(1) the person commits public mischief` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person acts with intent to mislead` AND `the person causes a peace officer to enter on or continue an investigation` AND (`by making a false statement that accuses some other person of having committed an offence` OR `by doing anything intended to cause some other person to be suspected of having committed an offence that the other person has not committed, or to divert suspicion from the person themselves` OR `by reporting that an offence has been committed when it has not been committed` OR `by reporting or in any other way making it known or causing it to be made known that the person or some other person has died when they have not died`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

